WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.900
An observational study of 120,000 older adults links bone drugs to 24% lower dementia risk. This is Longevity Weekly, Episode 8. The science of aging, read carefully, never medical advice. After that association, a high-dose flu analysis, an FDA eye warning on glp-1 drugs, and caloric restriction as the mechanism of the week. University of Hong Kong researchers in a study science daily describes an Alzheimer's and dementia, looked at

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:36.220
nitrogen containing bisphosphonates, drugs already used to slow bone loss and fractures. Patients

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:41.500
on those drugs were less likely to develop Alzheimer's and other dementias. The same group had

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.940
already found osteoporosis and fractures standing as independent dementia risks, and people

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.600
already living with dementia more likely to fall and break a bone. More than 55 million people

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:59.000
live with dementia worldwide, account the author's project toward $139 million by 2050.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:04.200
Shared risks in the right-up include older age, being female, and low activity.

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.960
The paper does not report any regulator approving these bone drugs to prevent dementia, and

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.440
a second use remains a possibility the author's name, not a cause they proved.

00:01:15.481 --> 00:01:21.581
UT Health used an analyst compared flu shots in adults 65 and older, nearly 200,000 of

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:26.861
them, and this analysis is not described as a randomized trial. People who got the

00:01:26.861 --> 00:01:33.841
high dose influenza vaccine had a nearly 55% lower Alzheimer's risk, set against a 40% reduction

00:01:33.841 --> 00:01:38.821
previously tied to the standard dose. That is a comparison of people who received a shot,

00:01:39.301 --> 00:01:43.761
so other differences between those groups stay in the picture. Nothing in the report says

00:01:43.761 --> 00:01:48.903
influenza vaccines are approved to prevent Alzheimer's. The Food and Drug Administration,

00:01:48.903 --> 00:01:55.103
6 days after this shows November 4th look at GLP1 evidence beyond weight loss, warned

00:01:55.103 --> 00:02:00.663
that these drugs carry a potential risk of non-arturitic anterior ischemic optic neuropathy.

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:05.203
Stat reports the agency required companies to tell patients and doctors.

00:02:05.863 --> 00:02:07.723
People sometimes call it an eye stroke.

00:02:08.223 --> 00:02:13.223
Insufficient blood flow to the optic nerve typically brings sudden vision loss, and severe

00:02:13.223 --> 00:02:17.363
cases can end in blindness, with no proven treatment named in the report.

00:02:17.363 --> 00:02:24.643
The agency said it started looking after a 2024 observational study linked ozempic and wagovi to the condition.

00:02:25.163 --> 00:02:29.503
These sources do not report GLP-1 drugs approved as a treatment for aging.

00:02:30.578 --> 00:02:34.918
Georgetown's Lombardi Comprehensive Cancer Center built a population simulation,

00:02:35.358 --> 00:02:41.818
reported by genetic engineering and biotechnology news and medical express as appearing in JAMA network open,

00:02:41.818 --> 00:02:47.738
To weigh curing breast cancer against faster biological aging, John Mandelblatt, the senior

00:02:47.738 --> 00:02:53.038
author, said women who have survived breast cancer, are the largest share of the 18.6 million

00:02:53.038 --> 00:02:55.078
cancer survivors in the United States.

00:02:55.618 --> 00:03:00.838
Some chemotherapy that lengthened survival also damages normal cells and organs, and that

00:03:00.838 --> 00:03:05.278
acceleration of biological age can last for years and stay invisible for years.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:10.038
Frailty, cognitive problems, and other aging diseases can arrive earlier.

00:03:10.038 --> 00:03:15.878
Swarnevo Sarkar, the lead author, said the model counts both the survival gain and the damage,

00:03:16.338 --> 00:03:21.578
including more senescent cells that have stopped dividing, resist death, and secrete molecules

00:03:21.578 --> 00:03:27.587
that inflame tissue. The authors say survivorship care might someday use that aging knowledge to

00:03:27.587 --> 00:03:32.587
look for drug or behavior interventions. The papers here do not test those interventions.

00:03:33.587 --> 00:03:39.767
Rentocertib, a TNIK inhibitor from Encilical Medicine, sits in a phase 2 trial for idiopathic

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:45.147
pulmonary fibrosis, and fight aging reports that several proteomic aging clocks read

00:03:45.147 --> 00:03:46.527
younger in that human data.

00:03:47.087 --> 00:03:49.467
The drug is described as anti-fibrotic.

00:03:49.887 --> 00:03:54.907
A younger clock is a biomarker shift, not a measured longer life, and these sources do

00:03:54.907 --> 00:03:56.427
not report approval for aging.

00:03:56.967 --> 00:04:02.067
The same note points to rapamycin and related molecules as already having sturdier evidence

00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:07.147
that they touch aging mechanisms to some degree, which is a contrast, not a finding from

00:04:07.147 --> 00:04:08.327
this fibrosis trial.

00:04:09.391 --> 00:04:14.861
Nature aging published on November 10th, a paper by Lee, Sha, Sun, Ja, and colleagues

00:04:14.861 --> 00:04:17.441
on mytovesicles in Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:17.861 --> 00:04:23.801
They use patient brain samples and mouse models, and they flag GGT1 as an enriched cargo

00:04:23.801 --> 00:04:25.741
implicated in driving pathology.

00:04:26.321 --> 00:04:28.941
Human tissue plus mice, not a treatment trial.

00:04:29.641 --> 00:04:35.561
Aging cell is where a review, covered by lifespan.io, lands on poor sleep and inflammaging

00:04:35.561 --> 00:04:36.701
making each other worse.

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:41.921
That is a reading of a large existing literature, not a new group of people enrolled to test

00:04:41.921 --> 00:04:42.681
a sleep fix.

00:04:43.221 --> 00:04:48.921
Also on the desk, Fight Aging describes glimphatic drainage of cerebrospinal fluid as falling

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:55.101
with age and falling harder in Alzheimer's, with a job clearing amyloid beta, alpha-synucleon,

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.041
tau, and TDP-43.

00:04:57.621 --> 00:05:02.801
A study written up by Neutraceutical Business Review found NAD in blood does not decline

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:07.381
with age, which that outlet says undercuts longevity claims built on a drop.

00:05:08.301 --> 00:05:13.301
Cepheranthine, a plant extract, is reported by fight aging as a new senolytic candidate,

00:05:13.681 --> 00:05:18.661
with the caveat that cheap candidates of this sort have not tended to produce compelling human data.

00:05:19.632 --> 00:05:24.152
Chaloric restriction, this week's mechanism, is eating less energy than you would freely,

00:05:24.672 --> 00:05:30.192
without malnutrition, and a 2012 review in the American Journal of Human Biology calls it the

00:05:30.192 --> 00:05:35.232
strongest environmental intervention known to delay aging and extend life across experimental

00:05:35.232 --> 00:05:41.252
organisms. That claim lives in animals and lab models. The reviewers treat aging as the

00:05:41.252 --> 00:05:46.512
biggest risk factor for many cancers, heart disease, and diabetes, and they hope the mechanism

00:05:46.512 --> 00:05:52.592
will someday point to treatments. They do not test one. A 2013 review in the Journal of

00:05:52.592 --> 00:05:58.172
Cardiopolmonary Rehabilitation and Prevention draws the line at intake well below free eating,

00:05:58.172 --> 00:06:04.032
at least 10% in people and at least 20% in animals. Across animal work and a

00:06:04.032 --> 00:06:08.532
thin set of human trials, those authors see a chance of slower cardiac aging

00:06:08.532 --> 00:06:13.232
and less atherosclerotic disease through blood pressure, lipids, inflammation,

00:06:13.512 --> 00:06:17.532
and maybe other roots. Those are intermediate risks, not years of life

00:06:17.532 --> 00:06:21.772
counted in people. They say human health effects are still not fully understood.

00:06:22.192 --> 00:06:26.232
That modest restriction inside a wider lifestyle program is likely to help

00:06:26.232 --> 00:06:31.332
heart health and people with extra weight because of those cardiometabolic effects, and that

00:06:31.332 --> 00:06:35.732
older adults and people with serious illness such as heart failure still need more study.

00:06:36.312 --> 00:06:39.052
The human experiment with the most weight here is calorie.

00:06:39.672 --> 00:06:44.612
The comprehensive assessment of the long-term effect of reducing intake of energy reported

00:06:44.612 --> 00:06:48.392
in 2015 in the journals of gerontology series A.

00:06:48.392 --> 00:06:57.532
Investigators randomized 218 non obese adults, ages 21 to 51, average body mass index 25.1,

00:06:58.112 --> 00:07:04.412
to two years aimed at 25% restriction or to eating freely. 82% of the restriction group

00:07:04.412 --> 00:07:11.492
finished and 95% of the comparison group. What they achieved was 11.7% restriction, not

00:07:11.492 --> 00:07:17.612
the 25% on the drawing board, and they kept off 10.4% of body weight. The free eating

00:07:17.612 --> 00:07:23.172
group barely changed weight, resting metabolic rate, adjusted for that weight change, fell

00:07:23.172 --> 00:07:28.772
more with restriction at 12 months and did not at 24. Core temperature barely separated

00:07:28.772 --> 00:07:35.072
the groups. The thyroid hormone triiodothyronine fell more with restriction at both 12 and 24

00:07:35.072 --> 00:07:40.732
months. The authors call sustained restriction feasible in non obese adults, and say the

00:07:40.732 --> 00:07:45.752
pattern on survival correlates hints at aging-related benefits that later human studies would

00:07:45.752 --> 00:07:49.192
still have to show. Nobody's lifespan was the end point.

00:07:49.772 --> 00:07:53.232
Rhesus monkeys sit closer to us than a mouse and still are not us.

00:07:53.752 --> 00:07:59.892
A 2026 cross-sectional study in skeletal muscle compared 18 animals on 30% restriction

00:08:00.222 --> 00:08:07.212
with 18 controls. Deep RNA sequencing of skeletal muscle-found metabolism, mitochondria, signaling,

00:08:07.712 --> 00:08:13.992
and oxidative stress genes up, an immune, matrix, apoptosis, and ribosomal RNA processing

00:08:13.992 --> 00:08:19.652
genes down. Alternative splicing was a major way restriction rewrote genes tied to muscle,

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:26.232
metabolism, and aging. The authors read that as preserved muscle, less degeneration, less inflammation,

00:08:26.732 --> 00:08:33.692
and mechanism shared across species. Human astrocytes in a dish in a 2025 scientific reports paper

00:08:33.692 --> 00:08:38.632
got the glycolysis inhibitor 2 deoxyglucose as a stand-in for restriction,

00:08:38.632 --> 00:08:45.452
Then an inflammatory hit from interleukin-1 beta, oxygen use and acidification fell, and

00:08:45.452 --> 00:08:51.312
TNF, IL-6 and C3 expression fell, with chromatin accessibility changing alongside.

00:08:52.032 --> 00:08:57.232
Taking glucose away and adding the ketone beta hydroxybutyrate, also tracked with lower

00:08:57.232 --> 00:09:00.072
cytokines, and the effects stacked with the inhibitor.

00:09:00.632 --> 00:09:05.272
The authors float glycolysis as a future lever on astrocyte inflammation in neurological

00:09:05.272 --> 00:09:05.972
disease.

00:09:05.972 --> 00:09:11.272
That is a cell model of a lab chemical, not a diet result, and nothing here calls

00:09:11.272 --> 00:09:17.392
two deoxyglucose and approved aging treatment. A 2007 review in the Journal of Nutrition

00:09:17.392 --> 00:09:23.052
is blunt about the animal ceiling. In rodents, more restriction meant more lifespan, and

00:09:23.052 --> 00:09:28.192
starting later meant less benefit. Their model said a man who began 30% restriction

00:09:28.192 --> 00:09:35.012
at 48 and held it to an expected death at 78 might gain 2.8 years. That figure is a projection

00:09:35.012 --> 00:09:39.692
from animal patterns, not account of men, restricted animals stayed hungry,

00:09:40.212 --> 00:09:44.652
neuroendocrine profiles matched ongoing hunger, and the author's doubt people

00:09:44.652 --> 00:09:48.952
could keep this up for decades without long support. They also leave open

00:09:48.952 --> 00:09:52.952
whether appetite suppressing drugs would copy the effect, or whether hunger

00:09:52.952 --> 00:09:57.892
itself is part of the machinery. Exercise and cold can cut energy too, they note.

00:09:58.432 --> 00:10:02.052
An animal's answer those deficits differently, with only a small

00:10:02.052 --> 00:10:07.112
lifespan mark. No paper in this set shows caloric restriction lengthening human life.

00:10:07.672 --> 00:10:14.472
The strongest finding remains that randomized trial of 218 nonobese adults. Near 12% restriction

00:10:14.472 --> 00:10:20.012
for two years was doable and moved some survival-linked markers, including a thyroid hormone,

00:10:20.532 --> 00:10:25.632
while the metabolic rate gap at one year had closed by two. These papers do not report

00:10:25.632 --> 00:10:30.852
any regulator approving caloric restriction as a medical treatment for aging, worth knowing

00:10:30.852 --> 00:10:35.452
from the human evidence, an association in people already on bone drugs is not proof

00:10:35.452 --> 00:10:36.872
those drugs guard the brain.

00:10:37.472 --> 00:10:42.772
An analysis of who received which flu shot is not a trial that vaccination prevents Alzheimer's.

00:10:43.252 --> 00:10:47.832
A simulation of breast cancer survivors can separate longer survival from later loss

00:10:47.832 --> 00:10:53.852
of healthy years, including damage from senescent cells, and two years of eating less in a randomized

00:10:53.852 --> 00:10:58.192
group of non-obese adults, shifted markers without ever measuring lifespan.

